# EAS Build archive exclusions.
#
# Why this file exists: the first build uploaded 102 MB. Every tracked file in
# the entire repository totals 1.5 MB. The only thing on disk large enough to
# account for the difference is mobile/node_modules (383 MB, which gzips to
# roughly 100 MB) — so it went into the archive despite being gitignored.
#
# EAS installs dependencies on the worker itself, so shipping node_modules is
# pure waste: it is compressed, uploaded, and then thrown away. Worse, these
# are Windows-resolved packages with Windows-specific optional binaries, which
# have no business on a Linux builder.
#
# IMPORTANT: when .easignore is present, EAS uses it INSTEAD of .gitignore, not
# in addition to it. So this file must be complete on its own — anything left
# out here gets uploaded, even if .gitignore excludes it.

# Dependencies — reinstalled on the worker
node_modules/

# Expo local state and build output
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
expo-env.d.ts
.metro-health-check*

# Generated native projects — EAS runs prebuild itself
/android
/ios
.kotlin/
*.orig.*

# Signing material must never leave this machine
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.pem
*.mobileprovision

# Local env
.env*.local

# Logs and caches
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
